   '{"participation_years": "2018-19", "current_location": "Austin, USA", "origin_location": "San Salvador, El Salvador", "languages": "Spanish, English", "current_role": "Student, B.S. Information Systems (senior) at a public university in Texas; part-time IT help desk technician, about 20 hours a week", "project": "We built a web app that maps free after-school meal sites in Austin and shows which are open right now. A local food bank gave us site data, and parents at two schools told us the old PDF list was impossible to read on a phone.", "since_technovation": "I went to a public university on a scholarship, switched from nursing to information systems after my first programming class, and got a campus help desk job. I’m now applying for data and analytics internships.", "impact": "It gave me something to put on my first resume when I had no internships and no one in my family who’d worked in tech.", "story_angles": "I’m the first person in my family to go to college, so I’ve figured out recruiting, resumes, and networking mostly on my own. I also help look after my two younger brothers, which shapes how I plan my week.", "interests": "Breaking into tech without connections, getting more first-gen students into data careers, and using data to improve access to food and other basics.", "skills": "SQL, Excel dashboards from my help desk job, JavaScript from the Technovation app, and explaining technical problems to non-technical people. I’m fully bilingual in English and Spanish.", "story_formats": ["Written profile or Q&A feature (newsletter, website, blog)", "Social media spotlight (LinkedIn, Instagram, etc.)"], "speaking_types": ["Speak as a panelist", "Virtual Events"], "topic_familiarity": {"Community Building": "Moderately experienced - I have some professional/project experience", "Tech Democratization": "Moderately experienced - I have some professional/project experience", "AI & Machine Learning (research, applications, ethics)": "Emerging interest - I''m