   '{"participation_years": "2013-14", "current_location": "Toronto, Canada", "origin_location": "Enugu, Nigeria", "languages": "English, Igbo", "current_role": "Senior Product Manager at a large e-commerce company; previously a software engineer", "project": "We built a web app that helps secondary school students in Enugu find and apply for scholarships, with deadline reminders. A teacher gave us a list of 80 scholarships, and about 20 students used the app to apply that year.", "since_technovation": "I studied computer science in Nigeria, moved to Canada for a master’s, worked as a software engineer for four years, then switched to product management. I now manage a team that builds checkout tools.", "impact": "It was the first time I presented to a room of adults, which made it easier to speak up in meetings later. It also showed me that I like deciding what to build, not only building it.", "story_angles": "I moved countries twice for school and work, and immigration paperwork shaped many of my career choices. I also switched from engineering to product and had to learn to be taken seriously without coding all day. I’m still the only Black woman on most teams I join.", "interests": "Breaking into product management, building products for emerging markets, and mentoring international students in Canada.", "skills": "Product strategy, roadmapping, SQL for analysis, user interviews, and managing stakeholders. I’ve also run internal workshops on writing product specs.", "story_formats": ["Written profile or Q&A feature (newsletter, website, blog)", "Podcast or audio interview", "Case study or impact report feature"], "speaking_types": ["Speak as a panelist", "Moderate panels and interviews", "Virtual Events", "In-Person Events"], "topic_familiarity": {"Leadership": "Deeply experienced - I work in this area professionally", "Career Transitions (academic -> industry, IC -> management, etc.)": "Deeply experienced - I work in this area professionally", "Engineering": "