   '{"participation_years": "2016-17", "current_location": "New York, USA", "origin_location": "Queens, New York, USA", "languages": "English, Bengali", "current_role": "Analyst at an investment bank", "project": "We built a web app that helps immigrant families in our neighborhood compare remittance fees and send money home at the lowest cost. We interviewed 40 families at a community center and found most didn’t know the fee until after they paid.", "since_technovation": "I studied economics at a public college on a full scholarship, interned at two banks, and now work as an analyst at an investment bank. I volunteer teaching financial literacy at the same community center where we tested our app.", "impact": "It showed me that finance and technology shape the lives of families like mine, and it’s why I wanted to work in finance. It also gave me the confidence to speak up in rooms where I was the youngest.", "story_angles": "I’m the first person in my family to work in finance, and one of few women of color on my team. At first I felt I had to prove I belonged, and I’m still learning to ask for what I need.", "interests": "Financial access for immigrant families, fintech for remittances, and finance careers for first-gen students.", "skills": "Financial modeling, Excel, SQL, valuation, and presenting analysis to senior bankers. I also teach budgeting workshops.", "story_formats": ["Written profile or Q&A feature (newsletter, website, blog)", "Social media spotlight (LinkedIn, Instagram, etc.)"], "speaking_types": ["Speak as a panelist", "Virtual Events"], "topic_familiarity": {"Career Transitions (academic -> industry, IC -> management, etc.)": "Moderately experienced - I have some professional/project experience", "Tech Democratization": "Moderately experienced - I have some professional/project experience", "AI & Machine Learning (research, applications, ethics)": "Emerging interest - I''m learning/transitioning into this area", "Entrepreneurship & Startups": "E